      {
        "id": 2614703,
        "name": "Sasha Nemtsov",
        "username": "Sasha_Nemtsov",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/sasha_nemtsov/{size}/393707_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-10-26T20:33:39.531Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This topic periodically appears on the Forum. There has not recently been any statement from CCP, that I’m aware of.</p>\n<p>Some folks have suggested that there might be technical difficulties involved, but I find that hard to accept.</p>\n<p>I have increasing difficulties with vision (ageing…) which cannot be addressed simply by using stronger spectacles. I use a large pointer in Windows and it transfers usefully to other software I have; but not to EVE.</p>\n<p>The developers could treat it as an Accessibility issue, and prioritise it in that way, but it’s entirely up to them. Perhaps…New CSM? New Pointer! Fingers crossed.</p>",
