      {
        "id": 2615004,
        "name": "Geo Eclipse Oksaras",
        "username": "Geo_Eclipse_Oksaras",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.eveonline.com/geo_eclipse_oksaras/{size}/500781_2.png",
        "created_at": "2024-10-27T12:23:38.703Z",
        "cooked": "<p>it’s legacy code that is deeply entwined into everything.</p>\n<p>The same reason POS’s are still around… any time CCP tries to remove them, or changes the code behind them…it breaks things elsewhere in the game in odd and horrifyingly unpredictable ways that make no real world sense.</p>\n<p>Meaning the code for the cursor is 20 some years old.  Most if not all the current devs aside ftom the ceo have no clue how the old code was written, or understand it, and it causes problems when they try to change it or customize it</p>\n<p>Weve had several player representatives for years try to get ccp to update it to no avail, because of how hard it is</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
